        "https://canny.io/images/a976e1dfc60b961f9305419d23b28865.png"
      ],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "653648aa7a2c635867434949",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is still an issue, nearly 5 months later.\n\nIssue is due to \"escaped\" characters not being reinterpreted.\n\n&[x]; is an HTML escape/entity syntax. It is a way of representing characters either by an entity name (e.g. `&nbsp;` is a *non-breaking space*), or by an identifier of some sort (e.g. `&#39;` or `&#x27;` for an apostrophe).\n\nThe problem is, specifically, that certain characters are being converted into HTML entity representations (likely for safety or security reasons; *input-sanitization*), but they are not correctly being *re-interpreted* as their original forms when displayed in a text container which (presumably) *does not* support HTML entities, such as the group/announcement title within VRChat or on the VRChat website (pictured).\n\nNote that, in this case, `&#39;` is an apostrophe's ***decimal*** representation, and not its true, ***hexadecimal***, unicode designation (`&#x27;`).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
